{"seconds": 38.7, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! After Rg2+ and any king move, the Black rook on f4 is completely undefended and White wins it with Kxf4. This is the key tactic.\n\n**Best move:** Rg2+\n\n**Main line:** Rg2+ Kh6 (or Kf5/Kh4) Kxf4, winning the rook.\n\n**Motif:** Deflection\n\n**Explanation:**\nYour opponent's rook on f4 is attacked only by your king and undefended\u2014a loose piece. The check Rg2+ forces the Black king away from defending it. After Kh6 (or any legal move), you simply play Kxf4, winning the rook outright. Always scan for loose pieces first; a check that forces your opponent's pieces farther away often wins material in one move.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rg2+\", \"line\": [\"Rg2+\", \"Kh6\", \"Kxf4\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\", \"hangingPiece\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57", "move": "Rxh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kR/5r2/4K3/P7/8 b - - 0 57", "move": "Kxh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57", "move": "Rg2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57", "move": "Rh4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P5R1/8 b - - 16 57", "move": "Rg4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57", "move": "Rg2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P5R1/8 b - - 16 57", "move": "Kf5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen":